Package: cockpit-samba-dc
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         acl,
         addcctl (= ${binary:Version}),
         cockpit-bridge (>= 337),
         ldb-tools,
         samba-ad-dc (>= 2:4.22),
         samba-common-bin,
Description: Cockpit module to manage a Samba Active Directory domain controller
 A Cockpit page that runs on the domain controller and manages users,
 groups, computers, home directories and shared folders, with network
 drives mapped at logon through a Group Policy Object.
 .
 It drives the local Samba tools (samba-tool, ldbsearch, net conf) as
 root through Cockpit and reads the directory from the local sam.ldb, so
 it needs no domain credentials.

Package: addcctl
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         acl,
         python3,
         python3-samba,
         samba-ad-dc (>= 2:4.22),
         samba-common-bin,
Description: operations of a Samba Active Directory domain controller, as JSON
 A command that runs on the domain controller, as root, and performs one
 operation per call: users, groups, computers, home directories, shared
 folders with their POSIX ACLs and the network drives mapped at logon
 through a Group Policy Object. It reads a JSON object on standard input
 and writes one on standard output; "addcctl mcp" offers the same
 operations as the tools of an MCP server.
 .
 It reads the directory from the local sam.ldb and the configuration from
 smb.conf, so it needs no domain credentials. It is the core of
 cockpit-samba-dc, used by its Cockpit page, its Ansible collection and
 its MCP server.
